message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "fpv_analysis: coupled simulation of floating photovoltaic lifetime performance in humid and saline conditions"
type: software
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-11-04
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/subrahmanyamtanala-rgb/Floating-Solar-Photovoltaic-System-for-Humid-and-Saline-Conditions"
authors:
  - family-names: Tanala
    given-names: Subrahmanyam
    affiliation: "Department of Electrical and Electronics Engineering, Anil Neerukonda Institute of Technology and Sciences (ANITS), Visakhapatnam, India"
    email: subrahmanyam.eee@anits.edu.in
keywords:
  - floating photovoltaics
  - PV degradation
  - humidity
  - salinity
  - simulation
  - uncertainty quantification
  - Sobol sensitivity analysis
abstract: >-
  Open-source hourly simulation framework for floating photovoltaic (FPV)
  systems in hot, humid and saline environments. One over-water microclimate
  drives module temperature, dew, dust and sea-salt soiling, and four module
  degradation mechanisms (intrinsic, Peck temperature-humidity, salt-assisted
  potential-induced degradation, chloride corrosion), feeding 25-year energy
  and levelized cost. Includes code-to-code verification against pvlib, Monte
  Carlo and Sobol uncertainty analysis, and scripts that reproduce every
  number, table and figure of the accompanying manuscripts.
